          },
          "worked": "There are $6\\times6=36$ equally likely ordered outcomes. Six doubles give $X=0$. For each positive difference $d$, there are $6-d$ pairs with the first die greater and $6-d$ with the second die greater.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(X=0)&=\\frac6{36}=\\frac16\\\\P(X=1)&=\\frac{10}{36}=\\frac5{18}\\\\P(X=2)&=\\frac8{36}=\\frac29\\\\P(X=3)&=\\frac6{36}=\\frac16\\\\P(X=4)&=\\frac4{36}=\\frac19\\\\P(X=5)&=\\frac2{36}=\\frac1{18}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThese probabilities sum to $1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 49
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the expected value of $X$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\mathrm E(X)=\\frac{35}{18}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm E(X)&=0\\times\\frac16+1\\times\\frac5{18}+2\\times\\frac29+3\\times\\frac16+4\\times\\frac19+5\\times\\frac1{18}\\\\\\mathrm E(X)&=\\frac{0+5+8+9+8+5}{18}\\\\\\mathrm E(X)&=\\frac{35}{18}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
